#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to update your code to use BackendV2 instead of BackendV1."
msgstr "Paano i-update ang iyong code para gamitin ang BackendV2 sa halip na BackendV1."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate from BackendV1 to BackendV2"
msgstr "Mag-migrate mula sa BackendV1 patungong BackendV2"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate from `BackendV1` to `BackendV2` {#migrate-from-backendv1-to-backendv2}"
msgstr "Mag-migrate mula sa `BackendV1` patungong `BackendV2` {#migrate-from-backendv1-to-backendv2}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Qiskit [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) class has been deprecated and will be removed from service. This migration guide describes the small adjustments you need to make if you use a provider that upgraded from [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) to [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2).\n"
msgstr "Ang Qiskit [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) class ay na-deprecate na at aalisin sa serbisyo. Inilalarawan ng migration guide na ito ang maliliit na pagbabagong kailangan mong gawin kung gumagamit ka ng provider na nag-upgrade mula sa [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) patungong [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
" If you exclusively use `qiskit_ibm_runtime` and `qiskit_aer`, no action is needed.  The `qiskit_ibm_runtime` package has always used `BackendV2`, and `qiskit_aer` has used `BackendV2` since version 0.13.\n"
" </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
" Kung eksklusibo kang gumagamit ng `qiskit_ibm_runtime` at `qiskit_aer`, walang kailangang gawin. Ang `qiskit_ibm_runtime` package ay palaging gumagamit ng `BackendV2`, at ang `qiskit_aer` ay gumagamit ng `BackendV2` simula pa sa bersyon 0.13.\n"
" </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "High-level changes in `BackendV2` {#high-level-changes-in-backendv2}"
msgstr "Mga pangunahing pagbabago sa `BackendV2` {#high-level-changes-in-backendv2}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Qiskit [`Backend`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.Backend) model was designed to provide the Qiskit SDK with an abstraction\n"
"layer that enabled reasoning about quantum computers within the scope of the SDK. The first iteration of the model was introduced with the\n"
"[`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) class. This class stored the backend information in a series\n"
"of data containers, namely the [`BackendConfiguration`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.models.BackendConfiguration) and\n"
"[`BackendProperties`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.models.BackendProperties) classes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Qiskit [`Backend`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.Backend) model ay idinisenyo para bigyan ang Qiskit SDK ng\n"
"abstraction layer na nagbibigay-daan sa pag-reason tungkol sa mga quantum computer sa loob ng saklaw ng SDK. Ang unang iterasyon ng\n"
"modelo ay ipinakilala gamit ang [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) class. Inimbak ng class na ito ang impormasyon ng backend sa isang serye ng\n"
"mga data container, partikular ang [`BackendConfiguration`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.models.BackendConfiguration) at\n"
"[`BackendProperties`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.models.BackendProperties) classes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) class redefined\n"
"user access for most backend properties to make them work with native Qiskit data structures and have flatter\n"
"access patterns. The core of the [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) model is the\n"
"[`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) class, a representation of the QPU that contains the transpilation constraints that Qiskit can use to optimize circuits for execution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Binago ng [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) class ang\n"
"paraan ng pag-access ng user sa karamihan ng backend properties para gumana ang mga ito kasama ang native na Qiskit data structures at magkaroon ng\n"
"mas simpleng access patterns. Ang pangunahing bahagi ng [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) model ay ang\n"
"[`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) class, isang representasyon ng QPU na naglalaman ng mga transpilation constraints na magagamit ng Qiskit para i-optimize ang mga circuit para sa execution.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Qiskit SDK has been updated to work exclusively with [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) inputs,\n"
"and most providers have upgraded from [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) to [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2). It is expected that existing providers will deprecate the old access where possible to provide a graceful migration, but eventually users will need to adjust their code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Na-update na ang Qiskit SDK para eksklusibong gumana kasama ang mga [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) input,\n"
"at karamihan sa mga provider ay nag-upgrade na mula sa [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) patungong [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2). Inaasahan na ang mga kasalukuyang provider ay mag-deprecate ng lumang access kung posible para sa maayos na migration, ngunit sa huli kailangang i-adjust ng mga user ang kanilang code.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The principle behind [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) is\n"
"that most of the information about a backend is contained in its\n"
"[`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) object, and the backend's attributes often query\n"
"its `BackendV2.target` attribute to return information. However, in many cases the attributes only provide\n"
"a subset of information that the target can contain. For example, `backend.coupling_map`\n"
"returns a [`CouplingMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap) constructed from the\n"
"[`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) accessible in the\n"
"`BackendV2.target` attribute. However, the target might contain\n"
"instructions that operate on more than two qubits (which can't be represented in a\n"
"[`CouplingMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap)) or it might have instructions that only operate on\n"
"a subset of qubits (or two qubit links, for a two qubit instruction), which won't be\n"
"detailed in the full coupling map returned by\n"
"`BackendV2.coupling_map`. So depending on your use case,\n"
"it might be necessary to look deeper than just the equivalent access with\n"
"[`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang prinsipyo ng [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) ay\n"
"ang karamihan ng impormasyon tungkol sa isang backend ay nasa loob ng\n"
"[`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) object nito, at ang mga attribute ng backend ay madalas na nagtatanong sa\n"
"`BackendV2.target` attribute para magbalik ng impormasyon. Gayunpaman, sa maraming kaso ang mga attribute ay\n"
"nagbibigay lamang ng subset ng impormasyong maaaring nakapaloob sa Target. Halimbawa, ang `backend.coupling_map`\n"
"ay nagbabalik ng [`CouplingMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap) object na itinayo mula sa\n"
"[`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) na accessible sa\n"
"`BackendV2.target` attribute. Gayunpaman, ang Target ay maaaring\n"
"maglaman ng mga instruction na gumagana sa higit sa dalawang qubit (na hindi maaaring i-represent sa\n"
"[`CouplingMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap)) o maaaring may mga instruction na gumagana lamang sa\n"
"isang subset ng mga qubit (o dalawang qubit link, para sa dalawang qubit na instruction), na hindi\n"
"makikita sa buong coupling map na ibinalik ng\n"
"`BackendV2.coupling_map`. Kaya depende sa iyong use case,\n"
"maaaring kailangan mong tumingin nang mas malalim kaysa sa katumbas na access gamit ang\n"
"[`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specific changes in `BackendV2` {#specific-changes-in-backendv2}"
msgstr "Mga partikular na pagbabago sa `BackendV2` {#specific-changes-in-backendv2}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Most attributes have a direct replacement, simplifying the migration efforts. The only point of mismatch between interfaces is in the [`CouplingMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap).\n"
msgstr "Karamihan sa mga attribute ay may direktang kapalit, na pinapasimple ang migration. Ang tanging punto ng hindi pagkakatugma sa pagitan ng mga interface ay nasa [`CouplingMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Following is a table of example access patterns in [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) and the new form\n"
"with [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2).\n"
msgstr ""
"Nasa ibaba ang isang talahanayan ng mga halimbawa ng access pattern sa [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) at ang bagong form\n"
"gamit ang [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"important\">\n"
"Scroll to the right to see important notes.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"important\">\n"
"I-scroll pakanan para makita ang mahahalagang tala.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|[`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) | [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) | Notes |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().n_qubits` | `backend.num_qubits`| |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().coupling_map` | `backend.coupling_map` | The return from [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) is a [`CouplingMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap) object. In [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) it is an edge list. Also, this is just a view of the information contained in `backend.target` which may only be a subset of the information contained in the [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) object. |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().backend_name` | `backend.name` | |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().backend_version` | `backend.backend_version` | The `BackendV2.version` attribute represents the version of the abstract [`Backend`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.Backend) interface that the object implements, while `BackendV2.backend_version` is metadata about the version of the backend itself. |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().basis_gates` | `backend.operation_names` | The [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) returns a list of operation names contained in the `backend.target` attribute. The [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) might contain more information than can be expressed by this list of names. For example, some operations only work on a subset of qubits, and some names implement the same gate with different parameters.|\n"
"|`backend.configuration().dt`|`backend.dt`| |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().dtm`|`backend.dtm` | |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().max_experiments` |`backend.max_circuits` | |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().online_date` | `backend.online_date`| |\n"
"|`InstructionDurations.from_backend(backend)`|`backend.instruction_durations`| |\n"
"|`backend.defaults().instruction_schedule_map`|`backend.instruction_schedule_map`| |\n"
"|`backend.properties().t1(0)`|`backend.qubit_properties(0).t1`| |\n"
"|`backend.properties().t2(0)`|`backend.qubit_properties(0).t2`| |\n"
"|`backend.properties().frequency(0)`|`backend.qubit_properties(0).frequency`| |\n"
"|`backend.properties().readout_error(0)`|`backend.target[\"measure\"][(0,)].error`| In [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2), the error rate for the [`Measure`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#measure) operation on a given qubit is used to model the readout error. However, a [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) object can implement multiple measurement types and list them separately in a [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target).|\n"
"|`backend.properties().readout_length(0)`|`backend.target[\"measure\"][(0,)].duration`| In [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2), the duration for the [`Measure`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#measure) operation on a given qubit is used to model the readout length. However, a [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) object can implement multiple measurement types and list them separately in a [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target).|\n"
msgstr ""
"|[`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) | [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) | Mga Tala |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().n_qubits` | `backend.num_qubits`| |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().coupling_map` | `backend.coupling_map` | Ang ibinalik mula sa [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) ay isang [`CouplingMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap) object. Sa [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) ito ay isang edge list. Gayundin, ito ay isang view lamang ng impormasyon na nasa `backend.target` na maaaring subset lamang ng impormasyon sa [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) object. |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().backend_name` | `backend.name` | |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().backend_version` | `backend.backend_version` | Ang `BackendV2.version` attribute ay kumakatawan sa bersyon ng abstract na [`Backend`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.Backend) interface na ipinapatupad ng object, habang ang `BackendV2.backend_version` ay metadata tungkol sa bersyon ng backend mismo. |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().basis_gates` | `backend.operation_names` | Ang [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) ay nagbabalik ng listahan ng mga operation name na nasa `backend.target` attribute. Ang [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) ay maaaring maglaman ng higit pang impormasyon kaysa sa maipapahayag ng listahang ito. Halimbawa, ang ilang operation ay gumagana lamang sa isang subset ng mga qubit, at ang ilang pangalan ay nagpapatupad ng parehong gate na may iba't ibang parameter.|\n"
"|`backend.configuration().dt`|`backend.dt`| |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().dtm`|`backend.dtm` | |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().max_experiments` |`backend.max_circuits` | |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().online_date` | `backend.online_date`| |\n"
"|`InstructionDurations.from_backend(backend)`|`backend.instruction_durations`| |\n"
"|`backend.defaults().instruction_schedule_map`|`backend.instruction_schedule_map`| |\n"
"|`backend.properties().t1(0)`|`backend.qubit_properties(0).t1`| |\n"
"|`backend.properties().t2(0)`|`backend.qubit_properties(0).t2`| |\n"
"|`backend.properties().frequency(0)`|`backend.qubit_properties(0).frequency`| |\n"
"|`backend.properties().readout_error(0)`|`backend.target[\"measure\"][(0,)].error`| Sa [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2), ang error rate para sa [`Measure`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#measure) operation sa isang partikular na qubit ang ginagamit para i-model ang readout error. Gayunpaman, ang isang [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) object ay maaaring mag-implement ng maraming uri ng measurement at ilista ang mga ito nang hiwalay sa isang [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target).|\n"
"|`backend.properties().readout_length(0)`|`backend.target[\"measure\"][(0,)].duration`| Sa [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2), ang duration para sa [`Measure`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#measure) operation sa isang partikular na qubit ang ginagamit para i-model ang readout length. Gayunpaman, ang isang [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) object ay maaaring mag-implement ng maraming uri ng measurement at ilista ang mga ito nang hiwalay sa isang [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target).|\n"
